2.3𝛼-Local Stability
Following the complexity of local-stability computation, we define an approximate version of the
problem. We start by defining an 𝛼-𝑘-stable zone boundary as a set of refinements that is a 𝑘-stable
boundary up to some error. Namely, the probability of sampling a 𝑘-unstable refinement from
the set of refinements under an 𝛼-𝑘-stable zone boundary is at most 𝛼when samples are drawn
