Definition 4.2 (Tuple-independent ranking function). A ranking function is tuple-independent if
for any𝑡∈𝐷and𝑡′obtained by refining 𝑡, and all𝑎,𝑏∈𝐷\{𝑡,𝑡′}such that𝑓(𝐷)[𝑎]<𝑓(𝐷)[𝑏],
then𝑓(𝐷𝑡→𝑡′)[𝑎]<𝑓(𝐷𝑡→𝑡′)[𝑏].
Tuple independence is a common feature of ranking functions. For instance, the scoring function
based on the geometric mean of attributes in Example 1.1 is tuple-independent, since altering the
attributes of one tuple only modifies the score of that tuple, leaving the relative ordering between
the rest of the tuples unchanged.
