We next examine the scalability of the optimized version of LStability (LSt) compared to the basic
version presented in Section 3 (Basic), and quantify the effect of our proposed optimizations.
Scalability .We evaluate the scalability of our methods with growing data sizes and numbers
of attributes using synthetic datasets. Figure 11 shows the runtime of both the optimized and
basic versions of LStability as a function of the data size. As expected, LSt outperforms Basic. We
observed a linear increase in the Basic’s running time, with increasing data size, while the impact on
